// A turbofish reflection query names a real type, so an unresolvable one is a checker error (E0013)
// — not a silently empty schema. The turbofish keeps `T` as a genuine type reference all the way
// through the linker (which is what makes it resolve to a *qualified* identity under a `namespace`),
// so it is resolved here exactly like any other type annotation, `attributes_of::<T>()` included.
//
// The runtime-string surface `field_specs_of(name)` stays lenient by design — its operand's value is
// only known at runtime, so an unknown name there is the empty list, never an error.
// expect: error E0013 at 14:26
// expect: exit 1
struct Todo {
    id: int
}

specs = field_specs_of::<Todoo>()
echo specs.len()
